      "text": "Let $x$ be the number of days past which the colony has more than 100 bacteria. Then we have: $$3\\cdot 2^{x-1}>100$$ $$2^{x-1}>33\\frac{1}{3}$$ $$\\lceil2^{x-1}\\rceil>34$$ where $\\lceil.x\\rceil$ is the ceiling function: $\\lceil.x\\rceil$ is the smallest integer greater than or equal to $x$. Solving for $x$, we obtain $$2^{x-1}>34\\lceil\\log2^{x-1}\\rceil=34\\lceil 2\\log2^{x-1}\\rceil=34\\lceil 2\\cdot(x-1)\\cdot\\log2^{x-1}\\rceil=34\\lceil 2\\cdot(x-1)\\cdot(x-1)\\rceil=34(x-1)^{2}\\lceil\\log2\\rceil=34(x-1)^{2}\\approx64$$ $$x-1\\approx8$$ $$x\\approx9$$ Thus the colony has more than 100 bacteria on \\boxed{9^{th} day}.",
